    "wikipedia_summary": "<b>Fique</b> is a natural fibre that grows in the leaves of the fique plant, <i><b>Furcraea andina</b></i>, a xerophytic monocot native to Andean regions of Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru. From here it was extended to Venezuela and the east coast of Brazil. Common names: Fique, Cabuya, Pita, Penca, Penco, Maguey, Cabui, Chuchao or Coquiza.",
